# Physics catalog, native receipt: the Arrange pane and the palette's physics
# rows are two doors onto one spine. Every choice is fired by palette label
# (what a person would pick) and read back off the pane's rows.
settle 40
act Open Arrange pane
settle 10
# The restored session's tree is busy; maximize so the captures read.
act Maximize pane
settle 5
assert maximized
assert row Arrangement:
assert row Physics: Springs
assert row Overlays: none
act Physics: Orbit
settle 10
assert row Physics: Orbit
assert row Profile: Orbit
act Overlay on: Skeleton
settle 5
assert row Overlays: Skeleton
assert row Profile: custom
act Overlay off: Skeleton
settle 5
assert row Overlays: none
act Profile: Crystal
settle 10
assert row Physics: Stress
assert row Overlays: Grid
assert row Profile: Crystal
capture 01_arrange_crystal
act Kinds: By colouring
act Mass: By rank
act Depth: By layer
settle 5
assert row Kinds: By colouring
assert row Mass: By rank
assert row Depth: By layer
act Layout: Force-directed
settle 5
assert row Arrangement: Free
act Physics: Still
settle 5
assert row Physics: Still
# A law switch keeps the overlays (Crystal's grid survives), so the pair is
# custom; the profile is what sets both.
assert row Overlays: Grid
assert row Profile: custom
act Profile: Void
settle 5
assert row Overlays: none
assert row Profile: Void
capture 02_arrange_still
log physics native receipt complete
